IMPORT prelude

-- Census and Statistics Act 1905 (Cth) -- the questions of the person asked to answer the Census or a statistical survey.
--
-- SEAT: the person (a householder, or a business) asked by the Australian Bureau of Statistics to fill in a form or answer a
-- question: "Must I fill this in?", "Which questions may I leave out?", "What can happen to me if I do not answer, or answer
-- falsely?", "Who may see what I give?".
--
-- Provisions covered: when a Census is taken (s 8); transfer of Census forms to the Archives with consent (s 8A); the ways the
-- Statistician may ask (ss 10, 11), with the 14-day minimum and the s 14 warning a direction must carry (ss 10(4)-(5), 11(2)-(3));
-- results that must not identify the person (s 12(2)); release under a determination and its limit for personal or domestic
-- information (s 13); the offence of not complying with a direction and its religion exception (s 14); false or misleading answers
-- (s 15); entry to premises (s 18); the officers' secrecy offence (s 19); the 99-year bar on giving Census forms to Agencies and
-- courts (s 19A); summary hearing of a s 19 offence (s 20); the continuing obligation (s 21); joinder and one penalty (s 22).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 9, compilation date 1 October 2020 (includes amendments up to Act No. 64, 2020), register id
-- C2020C00296, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1905A00015.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026 as the current
-- compilation). The Census and Statistics Regulation 2016 is NOT deposited: the matters it prescribes (other Census years, classes
-- of premises officers may enter, the Census topics) are INPUTS. The Census day is appointed by proclamation (s 8(2)) and the
-- Census requirement is made by notifiable instrument (s 10(2)); neither is deposited, so whether a person is in the instrument's
-- class is an INPUT. The dollar value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914, not deposited) is an INPUT.
--
-- NOT ENCODED (machinery, or addressed to others with no consequence for the person asked): external Territories (s 2);
-- arrangements with the States (s 6); the officers' undertaking (s 7); what the Statistician collects (s 9, beyond being a purpose);
-- publication duties and charges (s 12(1), (3)); appointment and delegation (ss 16, 17); former officers (s 19B); regulations
-- (s 27). Whether a company is a "person" is not settled by this Act (INFERENCE: the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, not deposited,
-- would answer it); the encoding treats the business in d048 as a person asked, and says so.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the person asked to answer, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Census and Statistics Act 1905 -- the person asked to answer`

§§ `s 8 -- when a Census is taken`

-- s 8(1): "The Census shall be taken in the year 1981 and in every fifth year thereafter, and at such other times as are
-- prescribed." (2): "The Census day shall be a day appointed for that purpose by proclamation."
@export Is a Census taken in this year (s 8(1))?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year
      `another time is prescribed for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe a Census at another time in that year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a Census taken in the year` IF
        (`year` AT LEAST 1981 AND (`year` MINUS 1981) MODULO 5 EQUALS 0)
    OR  `another time is prescribed for that year`

§§ `ss 10, 11 -- the ways I may be asked`

-- s 10(2): "For the purposes of section 8, the Statistician may, by notifiable instrument, require persons included in a specified
-- class of persons to fill up and supply ... the particulars specified in that form".
-- s 10(3), 11(1): "For the purposes of section 8 or 9, the Statistician or an authorized officer may, either orally or in
-- writing, request a person" to fill up a form, or to answer a question.
-- s 10(4), 11(2): "For the purposes of section 8 or 9, the Statistician may, by notice in writing served either personally or by
-- post on a person, direct the person" to fill up a form or answer a question "within such period after the service of the
-- notice, being not less than 14 days, as is specified in the notice". s 10(5), 11(3): the notice "shall set out the effect of
-- the provisions of section 14".

-- Method: how the Bureau asked me.
DECLARE Method IS ONE OF
    `the Census instrument under s 10(2)`
    `a request to fill up a form under s 10(3)`
    `a request to answer a question under s 11(1)`
    `a written direction to fill up a form under s 10(4)`
    `a written direction to answer a question under s 11(2)`
    `not asked at all`

-- Purpose: the Census (s 8) or other statistics (s 9), such as a business survey.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `the Census (s 8)`
    `other statistics (s 9)`

-- Asked: the facts of one approach to me -- the natural unit is one form or question put to one person.
DECLARE Asked HAS
    `how I was asked` IS A Method
    `what it is for` IS A Purpose
    `I am in the class the instrument specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days the notice gives me` IS A NUMBER
    `the notice sets out the effect of section 14` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since the notice was served` IS A NUMBER
    `I have complied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all I have left unanswered is about my religious beliefs` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What my position is, as I would want it told to me.
DECLARE Position IS ONE OF
    `I have not been validly asked, so nothing is required of me`
    `I am required by the Census instrument, but not answering is not itself an offence`
    `I am only requested, and not answering is not an offence`
    `I am directed, and not complying once the period runs is an offence (s 14)`
    `the notice falls short of s 10(4)-(5) or 11(2)-(3), so on this encoding not complying is not an offence`

-- Only the s 10(2) instrument is confined to the Census, and it reaches only the specified class; every other method serves s 8
-- or s 9.
@export Was I asked in a way the Act allows for this collection (ss 10, 11)?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Asked @desc How and why you were asked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I asked in a way the Act allows` IF
    CONSIDER `a`'s `how I was asked`
    WHEN `the Census instrument under s 10(2)` THEN
            `a`'s `what it is for` EQUALS `the Census (s 8)`
        AND `a`'s `I am in the class the instrument specifies`
    WHEN `not asked at all` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- INFERENCE: a notice that gives fewer than 14 days, or does not set out the effect of s 14, is read as not a direction "under
-- subsection 10(4) or 11(2)". The Act does not say what follows from a defective notice.
@export Was I served a direction that meets ss 10(4)-(5) or 11(2)-(3)?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Asked @desc How and why you were asked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I validly directed` IF
        (    `a`'s `how I was asked` EQUALS `a written direction to fill up a form under s 10(4)`
         OR  `a`'s `how I was asked` EQUALS `a written direction to answer a question under s 11(2)`)
    AND `a`'s `days the notice gives me` AT LEAST 14
    AND `a`'s `the notice sets out the effect of section 14`

@export Must I fill this in (ss 10, 11, 14)?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Asked @desc How and why you were asked
GIVETH A Position
DECIDE `Must I fill this in` IS
    IF (NOT `Was I asked in a way the Act allows` `a`)
    THEN `I have not been validly asked, so nothing is required of me`
    ELSE CONSIDER `a`'s `how I was asked`
         WHEN `the Census instrument under s 10(2)` THEN `I am required by the Census instrument, but not answering is not itself an offence`
         WHEN `a request to fill up a form under s 10(3)` THEN `I am only requested, and not answering is not an offence`
         WHEN `a request to answer a question under s 11(1)` THEN `I am only requested, and not answering is not an offence`
         OTHERWISE
            IF `Was I validly directed` `a`
            THEN `I am directed, and not complying once the period runs is an offence (s 14)`
            ELSE `the notice falls short of s 10(4)-(5) or 11(2)-(3), so on this encoding not complying is not an offence`

§§ `s 14 -- not answering`

-- s 14(1): "A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is served a direction under subsection 10(4) or 11(2); and (b) the
-- person fails to comply with the direction. Penalty: One penalty unit." (2): strict liability. Note 2: "A person commits an
-- offence in respect of each day until the person complies with the direction". (3): "Subsection (1) does not apply in relation
-- to a person's failure to answer a question, or to supply particulars, relating to the person's religious beliefs." (the
-- defendant bears an evidential burden).

-- Topic: what a question is about, so far as s 14(3) cares.
DECLARE Topic IS ONE OF
    `my religious beliefs`
    `any other matter`

@export Is this question one I may leave unanswered without ever committing the s 14 offence (s 14(3))?
GIVEN `the topic` IS A Topic @desc What the question is about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this question optional` IF
    `the topic` EQUALS `my religious beliefs`

-- INFERENCE: I "fail to comply" only once the period specified in the notice has run.
@export Has the period my direction gives me run out?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Asked @desc How and why you were asked, and how long ago
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my period run out` IF
    `a`'s `days since the notice was served` GREATER THAN `a`'s `days the notice gives me`

@export Have I committed an offence by not answering (s 14)?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Asked @desc How and why you were asked, and whether you have answered
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed an offence by not answering` IF
        `Was I validly directed` `a`
    AND `Has my period run out` `a`
    AND (NOT `a`'s `I have complied`)
    AND (NOT `a`'s `all I have left unanswered is about my religious beliefs`)

-- s 21: where a thing is required within a period under s 10(4) or 11(2), "the obligation ... continues, notwithstanding that that
-- period has expired ... until that act or thing is done". INFERENCE: one offence for each day after the period has run, counted
-- to the day asked about.
@export How many offences have I committed by not answering, counting one a day (s 14 Note 2, s 21)?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Asked @desc How and why you were asked, and how long ago
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many daily offences have I committed` IS
    IF `Have I committed an offence by not answering` `a`
    THEN `a`'s `days since the notice was served` MINUS `a`'s `days the notice gives me`
    ELSE 0

-- s 22(1): charges for offences against s 14 "may be joined ... if those offences relate to a failure to do the same act or
-- thing"; (2): one penalty may be imposed, but it "shall not exceed the sum of the maximum penalties" for each offence.
@export What is the most I can be fined for not answering, in penalty units, if the daily charges are joined (s 22)?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Asked @desc How and why you were asked, and how long ago
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not answering in penalty units` IS
    `How many daily offences have I committed` `a` TIMES 1

@export What is the most I can be fined for not answering, in dollars (s 22)?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Asked @desc How and why you were asked, and how long ago
      `the value of a penalty unit in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc The dollar value of one penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914), supplied by you
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not answering in dollars` IS
    `What is the most I can be fined for not answering in penalty units` `a` TIMES `the value of a penalty unit in dollars`

§§ `s 15 -- answering falsely`

-- s 15: a person commits an offence if (a) the person "is required, requested or directed to fill up and supply particulars under
-- subsection 10(2), (3) or (4)" or "is requested or directed to answer a question under subsection 11(1) or (2)"; (b) makes a
-- statement or provides a document in connection with it; and (c) "knows that the statement or information is false or
-- misleading in a material particular". Penalty: 10 penalty units.
-- Unlike s 14, s 15 reaches the Census instrument and a mere request. INFERENCE: a direction that falls short of s 10(5) or 11(3)
-- is still a direction for s 15, since s 15 is not tied to the notice's contents.
@export Is a false answer I gave an offence (s 15)?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Asked @desc How and why you were asked
      `I made a statement or gave a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you answered, orally or in writing, or handed over a document
      `I knew it was false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knew it was false or misleading on a point that matters
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my false answer an offence` IF
        `Was I asked in a way the Act allows` `a`
    AND `I made a statement or gave a document`
    AND `I knew it was false or misleading in a material particular`

§§ `ss 14, 15, 19, 20 -- the maximum penalties`

-- s 14: "One penalty unit". s 15: "10 penalty units". s 19(1), (3): "120 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years, or both".
-- s 20(1): offences other than s 19 "shall be prosecuted summarily"; (3): a s 19 offence heard summarily: "imprisonment for a
-- period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 20 penalty units, or both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `my not complying with a direction (s 14)`
    `my false or misleading answer (s 15)`
    `an officer passing on what I gave, on indictment (s 19)`
    `an officer passing on what I gave, heard summarily (s 19, s 20(3))`

@export What is the most that can be fined for this offence, in penalty units (ss 14, 15, 19, 20)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc The offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most that can be fined in penalty units` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `my not complying with a direction (s 14)` THEN 1
    WHEN `my false or misleading answer (s 15)` THEN 10
    WHEN `an officer passing on what I gave, on indictment (s 19)` THEN 120
    WHEN `an officer passing on what I gave, heard summarily (s 19, s 20(3))` THEN 20

@export What is the longest imprisonment for this offence, in months (ss 14, 15, 19, 20)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc The offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an officer passing on what I gave, on indictment (s 19)` THEN 24
    WHEN `an officer passing on what I gave, heard summarily (s 19, s 20(3))` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `s 18 -- entry to my premises`

-- s 18(1): the Statistician or an authorized officer "may, at all reasonable times, enter any premises included in a prescribed
-- class of premises" to supply or collect forms and make inquiries. (2): premises means premises other than "(a) a dwelling-house
-- (including a flat or home unit); or (b) a part of any other premises that is separately occupied or used for the purposes of the
-- residence or sleeping accommodation of a person or persons". The prescribed classes are in the Regulation, not deposited: INPUT.
DECLARE Premises IS ONE OF
    `a dwelling-house`
    `a flat or home unit`
    `a part separately used for residence or sleeping`
    `business premises`

@export May an officer of the Bureau enter my premises (s 18)?
GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises @desc What kind of premises
      `the premises are in a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe the class your premises fall in
      `at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the officer comes at a reasonable time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May an officer enter my premises` IF
        `the premises are in a prescribed class`
    AND `at a reasonable time`
    AND CONSIDER `the premises`
        WHEN `business premises` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 12, 13, 19 -- who may see what I give`

-- s 12(2): results "shall not be published or disseminated in a manner that is likely to enable the identification of a
-- particular person or organization".
@export May published results identify me or my organisation (s 12(2))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May published results identify me` IS FALSE

-- s 13(1): the Minister may by legislative instrument make determinations for disclosure, "with the approval in writing of the
-- Statistician", of a specified class of information; (2)(b) a determination may name persons "whose consent is required";
-- (3): "Information of a personal or domestic nature relating to a person shall not be disclosed in accordance with a
-- determination in a manner that is likely to enable the identification of that person." Whether a determination covers the
-- information, and what it requires, are INPUTS.
@export May what I gave be released to someone under a s 13 determination?
GIVEN `a determination covers the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial determination under s 13 covers this class of information
      `the Statistician approved in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Statistician approved the release in writing
      `the determination requires my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the determination requires your consent
      `I consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consented
      `it is personal or domestic information about me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is of a personal or domestic nature about you
      `the release is likely to identify me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the release is likely to enable you to be identified
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my information be released under a determination` IF
        `a determination covers the information`
    AND `the Statistician approved in writing`
    AND ((NOT `the determination requires my consent`) OR `I consented`)
    AND (NOT (`it is personal or domestic information about me` AND `the release is likely to identify me`))

-- s 19(1): an offence if the person "is, or has been, the Statistician or an officer" and "divulges or communicates to another
-- person (other than the person from whom the information was obtained) any information given under this Act". (2): not if "(a)
-- in accordance with a determination under section 13; or (b) for the purposes of this Act".
@export Would an officer commit an offence by passing on what I gave (s 19)?
GIVEN `the one passing it on is or was the Statistician or an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is or was the Statistician or an officer of the Bureau
      `it went to someone other than me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was passed to someone other than you
      `it was under a section 13 determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was released under a s 13 determination
      `it was for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was for the purposes of the Census and Statistics Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would an officer commit an offence by passing on what I gave` IF
        `the one passing it on is or was the Statistician or an officer`
    AND `it went to someone other than me`
    AND (NOT `it was under a section 13 determination`)
    AND (NOT `it was for the purposes of this Act`)

§§ `s 19A -- the 99-year bar`

-- s 19A(1), (2): the Statistician or an officer "must not, at any time during the period of 99 years beginning on the Census day
-- for a Census" be required to divulge, or voluntarily give, information in a Census form to an Agency (other than in accordance
-- with this Act), or to a court or tribunal. (3): "Census day ... means the day appointed, under subsection 8(2)".
-- INFERENCE: the period beginning on the Census day ends the day before its 99th anniversary (29 February not handled).
@export Is my Census form shielded from government agencies and the courts on this date (s 19A)?
GIVEN `the Census day` IS A NUMBER @desc The Census day, YYYYMMDD
      `the date asked about` IS A NUMBER @desc The date you are asking about, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my Census form shielded from agencies and courts` IF
        `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the Census day`
    AND `the date asked about` LESS THAN `the Census day` PLUS 990000

§§ `s 8A -- the Archives`

-- s 8A: if a form is given under s 10 "in relation to the Census taken in the year 2001 or a later year" and "a person has
-- consented, in accordance with the form" to transfer to the Archives, "the Statistician must transfer the information".
@export Will my Census form be kept in the National Archives (s 8A)?
GIVEN `the Census year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the Census
      `I consented on the form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you ticked consent on the form
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my Census form go to the Archives` IF
    `the Census year` AT LEAST 2001 AND `I consented on the form`
